  "title": "2026-09-08-outline-123806 · code-review-agents",
  "description": "# Multi-agent automated code review\n\nRead left to right through five stages: intake, context and planning, concurrent reviewers, merge and verification, then publication and calibration.\n\n- Intake resolves the diff, files, review policy and build status; rejects drafts and excludes generated or vendored paths before model work.\n- Context is ranked and truncated to budget, with dropped material logged. The planner partitions review units over shared context for correctness, security, performance, test-coverage and API-compatibility agents.\n- Reviewers use bounded read-only tools and return available findings on budget exhaustion. Findings carry a current-file location, severity, rationale and confidence.\n- Aggregation deduplicates, reconciles severity, withholds low confidence and removes stale locations. High-severity findings are rechecked against source; unverified findings are demoted, not posted.\n- Surviving findings become inline comments and a policy-driven verdict. Author replies and human disagreements calibrate later per-class confidence thresholds, recording findings resolved as wrong.\n\nThe lower lifecycle-control region documents cancellation and restart on head changes, discarding partial work; repository tools and call budgets; and telemetry for cost, latency, reviewer tokens, cancellations and accepted versus dismissed findings. Dashed red is cancellation/restart, orange is daily-budget degradation to correctness and security only, and blue is calibration feedback. Section-level dispatch and results edges represent the concurrent reviewer group, not a sequential chain.",
